<https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1903-04/page/134> a crm:E22_Man-Made_Object,
        mbdiaries-ontology:Page ;
    rdfs:label "134"^^xsd:string ;
    crm:P129i_is_subject_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/diary/1903-04/document/134> ;
    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493312404/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Mr.
Story was as polite as pie to Bernhard, evidently regarding him as the future Director. Came home to a “tea” - Senda and Bessie, the Halls, Gans, Mr. Reynolds and Mr. Percy Griffin. Dined with the Steins, such well-meaning horrible Jews, and Gans took his cousin Mr. Sternberger and me to Zangwill’s play, “Merely Mary Ann.” It was very poor, I thought, just the Situation, and the characters running in the grooves cut for them by the situation. After the play, when I was dying to get home, Mr. Gans took us to Delmonico’s and spent $10.00 on making us eat and drink things none of us wanted. The spree must have cost him $25.00 at least, for he had a carriage. I hate that way of doing things. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 134 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1903-04> .

